#CHLOEAI:1
TYPE="path_rules"
GLOB="src/**, include/**"

LANGUAGE_RUNTIME:
- C99 dialect via SDCC compiler (Small Device C Compiler)
- GBDK-2020 fork (https://github.com/gbdk-2020/gbdk-2020) — pin version in Makefile (e.g., "4.2.0")
- Target hardware: Game Boy (DMG), Game Boy Color (CGB), Game Boy Advance (AGB) — declare target in build flags

BUILD:
- make (Makefile drives lcc → SDCC → linker → ROM output)
- Output: .gb or .gbc ROM file in build/ or bin/
- Type-check / lint: SDCC warnings should be zero — treat warnings as errors via -Werror equivalent
- Sanity-check ROM size: Game Boy cartridges have hard limits (32 KB MBC0, up to 8 MB MBC5)

STYLE_CONVENTIONS:
- File extension: .c for source, .h for headers
- Use uint8_t / uint16_t (from stdint.h) — not int (16-bit on Game Boy, surprising)
- Sprite/tile data lives in src/data/ or assets/ as binary or PNG → tile converter
- Bank organization: declare with #pragma bank N — overflow across banks is silent corruption
- Use BANKREF + BANKREF_EXTERN for cross-bank function calls

FORBIDDEN_PATTERNS:
- No floating point — Game Boy has no FPU, SDCC emulates via huge software routines
- No malloc/free — there is no heap; use static buffers
- No printf in shipping code — bloats ROM massively (use display_text or sprite-based UI)
- No int without explicit size — assume 16-bit unless you know
- No global variables in WRAM without bank declaration
- No standard library calls outside of <gb/gb.h>, <gb/cgb.h>, and explicit GBDK headers

EXPLICITLY_NOT_TOUCHING:
- (fill in: generated tile data, sound bank assemblies, vendored GBDK headers, etc.)
- build/ output — regenerate from source
